CloudBurrow patch 10 to github.com/goccy/googlesqlite v0.3.1
(cloudburrow/cloudburrow#1061; the bug: #1120).

The bug: every comparison of two INTERVAL values, `SELECT INTERVAL 1 DAY =
INTERVAL 1 DAY` or `WHERE v = @p` of an INTERVAL column, failed
"unsupported eq operator for interval value", although an INTERVAL is a
comparable type in BigQuery ("All data types are supported except for:
GEOGRAPHY JSON ARRAY"). The patch compares two intervals as GoogleSQL does,
by their length, a month counting 30 days and a day 24 hours
(googlesql/public/interval_value.h, IntervalValue::GetAsNanos and its
comparison operators): INTERVAL 1 MONTH = INTERVAL 30 DAY. It needs patch 9
for the sign of a short negative interval. interval_compare_test.go fails
without the patch and passes with it; the module's own
value_interval_test.go, which held comparisons unsupported, now holds them
by length.

